% A statement the REPL cannot accept reports and the prompt comes back
% (PLAN.md section 10): a syntax error, two bad string literals, an assertion,
% a rule, an unsafe query, a run-time type error and an unknown command in
% turn, after each of which the session is still there to answer.
%
% Nothing a rejected statement touched survives it.  newp/1 is still undefined
% when the query on the next line asks for it, although the rule above marked
% it defined on its way to being rejected, and the .stats at the end still
% counts the program's two predicates and two rules.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
